# ref-9f998c8-complex-hull
# A complex hull (32 pseudo-random points on a sphere, b3CreateComplexHull seed 42,
# radius 0.5) dropped onto a flat ground box, 120 steps at fixed dt=1/60, 4 substeps,
# no wall clock.
# Reference: vanilla float box3d at upstream commit 9f998c8.
# Fixed: fixed3d on this branch (b3CreateComplexHull ported). The generated fixed hull
#   differs from the float hull by construction: the /65535.0f coordinate map is
#   quantized to Q48.16, so the generator produces the same point-count class (~32
#   vertices, same LCG seed) but not the same exact vertices.
# Observable: the dropped hull's resting height (lowest vertex y) and its contact count
#   after 120 steps.
# Tolerance: resting height within 0.05 m and contact count equal, stated as twice the
#   measured maximum divergence once the reference harness (tools/reference/, from card
#   fixed3d-box3d-reference-harness) is present at the base; that harness is absent at
#   BASE sprint/fixed3d-box3d-ports (8f51d2d), so this scene is added for its glob and
#   the ctest -L reference run is reported not-done in the port record until it lands.
# Fixed-point divergence (by design, CLAUDE.md c37cfe4 record): the engine is Q48.16
#   fixed point with the exact-SAT structure and no float SIMD hull core, so transform
#   traces are not bit-identical to float; the hull must still settle to the same
#   resting configuration within the stated tolerance.
scene ref-9f998c8-complex-hull
hull_generator complex 42
body hull position 0 5 0 density 1.0
body box half 10 0.5 10 position 0 -0.5 0 static
steps 120 dt 1/60 substeps 4
expect contactCount >= 1
expect restingY > -0.5
